---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Changelog — Golem"
  description="What shipped in Golem, release by release. v0.1: first public release — three modes, the Studio plugin, checkpoints, native undo and the Sparks free tier."
>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="cl-title">
    <div class="wrap changelog-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Changelog</p>
      <h1 id="cl-title">Carved in order</h1>
      <p class="lede">Every release, what it actually does, no adjectives doing heavy lifting.</p>

      <article class="release card card--seam" data-reveal aria-labelledby="rel-0-1">
        <header class="release-head">
          <h2 id="rel-0-1"><span class="release-tag">v0.1</span> First public release</h2>
          <p class="release-date">2026</p>
        </header>

        <p>
          Golem opens its doors. This release is the full describe-to-build loop: a web workspace,
          a real Studio plugin, and an agent that changes your actual place — carefully.
        </p>

        <h3>The workspace</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Chat-driven building with live streaming responses and a visible tool trace — you see every <code>get_project_tree</code>, <code>edit_script</code> and <code>run_and_check</code> as it happens.</li>
          <li>Three modes: <strong>Clay</strong> (1 spark — fast answers and small edits), <strong>Stone</strong> (4 sparks — features across your project), <strong>Rune</strong> (10 sparks — plans, builds, tests and fixes autonomously).</li>
          <li>Unlimited projects per account, each with its own chat history and memory of what you built.</li>
          <li>Image attachments — paste a screenshot of the bug, not a description of it.</li>
          <li>A stop button that actually stops the agent mid-run.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Golem for Studio (plugin)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Pairing by short-lived code (<code>GLM-XXXXXX</code>, 10-minute expiry) — no tokens to copy around.</li>
          <li>Reads and searches your scripts, edits them through Studio's own script editor APIs.</li>
          <li>Creates, moves, configures and deletes instances with typed, validated operations.</li>
          <li>Wraps every operation batch in a ChangeHistory waypoint — native <kbd>Ctrl+Z</kbd> undo.</li>
          <li>Starts and stops run mode, captures logs, and reports results back for verification.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Safety net</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Automatic checkpoint before every agent run; manual checkpoints on demand.</li>
          <li>One-click restore of any checkpoint — scripts and instances — even across sessions.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>The deal</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Free tier: 80 Sparks per day, hard quota, resets daily, no card ever collected.</li>
          <li>Pro (400 Sparks/day, priority queue, extended checkpoints) opens as a waitlist.</li>
          <li>Private projects are never used to train models.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <p class="changelog-foot" data-reveal>
        Watching this page? Golem is in active development — expect the next entry sooner than you
        think.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .changelog-wrap {
    max-width: 800px;
  }

  .release {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding: 2.2rem;
  }

  .release-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .release-head h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .release-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--amber);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 180, 84, 0.45);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem;
    margin-right: 0.6rem;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }

  .release-date {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .release h3 {
    margin-top: 1.8rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--amber);
  }

  .release ul {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.45rem;
  }

  .release li::marker {
    color: var(--amber);
  }

  .release strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .changelog-foot {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
</style>
